\pard\sl240\slmult1\f0\fs22\lang9\u-10179?\u-9000?\f1  EPISODE 1 \f2\emdash\f1  What Attachment Really Is\par
Key Message\par
Attachment is the bond that tells a child: \ldblquote You are safe with me.\rdblquote\par
\par
What This Means for Your Child\par
They need emotional closeness to feel secure.\par
\par
Attachment grows through small, everyday moments.\par
\par
Warmth, presence, and comfort build trust.\par
\par
Attachment is not about perfection \f2\emdash\f1  it\rquote s about connection.\par
\par
Try This at Home\par
Make warm eye contact during daily routines.\par
\par
Offer gentle touch (if your child is comfortable).\par
\par
Sit close during play or quiet time.\par
\par
Use a soft, steady voice.\par
\par
Reflection Questions\par
What moments help my child feel close to me?\par
\par
How do I show my child they are safe with me?\par
\par
Notes\par
(Blank space)\par
