\f0\u-10179?\u-9000?\f1  EPISODE 2 \f2\emdash\f1  Secure vs Insecure Attachment\par
Key Message\par
Children behave differently depending on how safe they feel.\par
\par
What This Means for Your Child\par
Secure attachment looks like confidence and curiosity.\par
\par
Insecure attachment may look like clinginess, avoidance, or confusion.\par
\par
These patterns are protective, not \ldblquote bad behaviour.\rdblquote\par
\par
Your consistency helps shift insecure patterns toward security.\par
\par
Try This at Home\par
Respond to your child\rquote s needs quickly and calmly.\par
\par
Offer comfort without judgment.\par
\par
Keep routines predictable.\par
\par
Stay emotionally available.\par
\par
Reflection Questions\par
How does my child seek comfort?\par
\par
What helps them feel secure?\par
\par
Notes\par
(Blank space)\par
\par
\f0\u-10179?\u-9000?\f1  EPISODE 3 \f2\emdash\f1  How Trauma Disrupts Attachment\par
Key Message\par
Trauma teaches children that adults may not be safe.\par
\par
What This Means for Your Child\par
They may push you away to protect themselves.\par
\par
They may cling tightly when scared.\par
\par
They may shut down or avoid closeness.\par
\par
These reactions are survival strategies.\par
\par
Try This at Home\par
Stay steady when your child pulls away.\par
\par
Offer connection without pressure.\par
\par
Use soft, predictable routines.\par
\par
Validate their feelings gently.\par
\par
Reflection Questions\par
How does my child react when stressed?\par
\par
How can I show them I\rquote m safe and consistent?\par
\par
Notes\par
(Blank space)\par
\par
\f0\u-10179?\u-9000?\f1  EPISODE 4 \f2\emdash\f1  Why Children Test for Safety\par
Key Message\par
Testing is a child\rquote s way of asking: \ldblquote Will you stay?\rdblquote\par
\par
What This Means for Your Child\par
Testing is not defiance \f2\emdash\f1  it\rquote s fear.\par
\par
They are checking if you are reliable.\par
\par
They need to know you won\rquote t leave when things get hard.\par
\par
Testing decreases when trust increases.\par
\par
Try This at Home\par
Stay calm during testing behaviours.\par
\par
Follow through on boundaries.\par
\par
Offer reassurance: \ldblquote I\rquote m here. I\rquote m not going anywhere.\rdblquote\par
\par
Keep your tone warm and steady.\par
\par
Reflection Questions\par
When does my child test me most?\par
\par
How can I respond with calm consistency?\par
\par
Notes\par
(Blank space)\par
\par
\f0\u-10179?\u-9000?\f1  EPISODE 5 \f2\emdash\f1  Connection Before Correction\par
Key Message\par
Children learn best when they feel connected.\par
\par
What This Means for Your Child\par
They need to feel understood before they can listen.\par
\par
Connection reduces power struggles.\par
\par
Emotional safety opens the door to learning.\par
\par
Correction without connection feels like rejection.\par
\par
Try This at Home\par
Get down to their eye level.\par
\par
Use a soft voice: \ldblquote I\rquote m listening.\rdblquote\par
\par
Validate feelings before teaching.\par
\par
Offer a hug or gentle touch.\par
\par
Reflection Questions\par
How do I connect before correcting?\par
\par
What helps my child feel understood?\par
\par
Notes\par
(Blank space)\par
\par
\f0\u-10179?\u-9000?\f1  EPISODE 6 \f2\emdash\f1  Repairing Attachment Ruptures\par
Key Message\par
Repair matters more than perfection.\par
\par
What This Means for Your Child\par
Ruptures happen in every relationship.\par
\par
What heals is returning, apologising, and reconnecting.\par
\par
Repair teaches emotional safety.\par
\par
Children learn trust through repair.\par
\par
Try This at Home\par
Say: \ldblquote I\rquote m sorry. I shouldn\rquote t have yelled.\rdblquote\par
\par
Reconnect with a hug or gentle touch.\par
\par
Talk about feelings after calm returns.\par
\par
Create a small ritual after repair (story, cuddle, walk).\par
\par
Reflection Questions\par
How do I repair after conflict?\par
\par
What helps my child reconnect with me?\par
\par
Notes\par
(Blank space)\par
\par
\f0\u-10179?\u-9000?\f1  EPISODE 7 \f2\emdash\f1  Building Trust Through Consistency\par
Key Message\par
Trust grows through repeated safe moments.\par
\par
What This Means for Your Child\par
They need predictable responses.\par
\par
They learn trust through your follow\f3\_\f1 through.\par
\par
Small consistent actions matter more than big gestures.\par
\par
Consistency reduces anxiety.\par
\par
Try This at Home\par
Keep routines steady.\par
\par
Follow through on promises.\par
\par
Use the same calm tone during stress.\par
\par
Create daily connection rituals.\par
\par
Reflection Questions\par
What consistent actions can I take daily?\par
\par
How do I show reliability to my child?\par
\par
Notes\par
(Blank space)\par
\par
\f0\u-10179?\u-9000?\f1  EPISODE 8 \f2\emdash\f1  Attachment Through Play\par
Key Message\par
Play is the language of connection.\par
\par
What This Means for Your Child\par
Play helps them feel seen and valued.\par
\par
It strengthens your bond.\par
\par
It helps them express emotions safely.\par
\par
Even 10 minutes a day makes a difference.\par
\par
Try This at Home\par
Let your child lead the play.\par
\par
Follow their ideas.\par
\par
Put your phone away.\par
\par
Use play to reconnect after conflict.\par
\par
Reflection Questions\par
What play does my child enjoy most?\par
\par
How can I make time for connection?\par
\par
Notes\par
(Blank space)\par
\par
\f0\u-10179?\u-9000?\f1  EPISODE 9 \f2\emdash\f1  Attachment Through Daily Rituals\par
Key Message\par
Small rituals create big safety.\par
\par
What This Means for Your Child\par
Rituals anchor their sense of belonging.\par
\par
They reduce anxiety and build predictability.\par
\par
They strengthen your bond.\par
\par
Rituals don\rquote t need to be fancy \f2\emdash\f1  just consistent.\par
\par
Try This at Home\par
Morning hug\par
\par
Bedtime story\par
\par
Shared meal\par
\par
\ldblquote Goodnight\rdblquote  phrase\par
\par
After\f3\_\f1 school check\f3\_\f1 in\par
\par
Reflection Questions\par
What rituals do we already have?\par
\par
What new ritual can I add this week?\par
\par
