\f0\u-10179?\u-9000?\f1  EPISODE 10 \f2\emdash\f1  Attachment With Teens\par
Key Message\par
Teens still need connection \f2\emdash\f1  just differently.\par
\par
What This Means for Your Child\par
Teens may pull away but still need emotional safety.\par
\par
They need respect, space, and presence.\par
\par
Listening builds trust.\par
\par
Connection looks like interest, not control.\par
\par
Try This at Home\par
Ask open\f3\_\f1 ended questions.\par
\par
Listen without interrupting.\par
\par
Respect their privacy.\par
\par
Offer support without pressure.\par
\par
Reflection Questions\par
How does my teen show they need connection?\par
\par
How can I stay present without overwhelming them?\par
\par
Notes\par
(Blank space)\par
\par
\f0\u-10179?\u-9000?\f1  EPISODE 11 \f2\emdash\f1  Attachment When You\rquote re Stressed\par
Key Message\par
Your calm helps your child feel safe.\par
\par
What This Means for Your Child\par
They feel your stress.\par
\par
They need your emotional stability.\par
\par
Self\f3\_\f1 regulation supports co\f3\_\f1 regulation.\par
\par
Small resets help you stay grounded.\par
\par
Try This at Home\par
Take 3 slow breaths before responding.\par
\par
Step outside for 1 minute of fresh air.\par
\par
Drink water regularly.\par
\par
Ask for help when needed.\par
\par
Reflection Questions\par
What stresses me most?\par
\par
How does my stress affect my child?\par
\par
Notes\par
(Blank space)\par
\par
\f0\u-10179?\u-9000?\f1  EPISODE 12 \f2\emdash\f1  Long\f3\_\f1 Term Attachment Healing\par
Key Message\par
Healing happens through repeated safe moments.\par
\par
What This Means for Your Child\par
Attachment healing is slow and gentle.\par
\par
Small daily moments matter more than big ones.\par
\par
Warmth, consistency, and presence build trust.\par
\par
Progress is slow but real.\par
\par
Try This at Home\par
Create daily connection rituals.\par
\par
Offer warmth even during hard moments.\par
\par
Celebrate small steps forward.\par
\par
Stay steady and predictable.\par
\par
Reflection Questions\par
What small moments can I create today?\par
\par
How has my child grown recently?\par
\par
Notes\par
